## Phase 4 — Failure Analysis (3–4 days)

> Goal: Move from "what's the accuracy?" to "why did it fail?"

### 4.1 Failure Taxonomy with Trace Capture

Auto-categorize each incorrect run into failure modes + store structured traces.

**Failure modes** (deterministic, rule-based):
| Mode | Detection Rule |
|---|---|
| `format_error` | Output doesn't match expected format (empty, truncated, raw JSON) |
| `hallucination` | Low faithfulness score (< 0.3) on RAG experiments |
| `incomplete` | Output significantly shorter than expected |
| `off_topic` | Low semantic similarity (< 0.2) with expected answer |
| `timeout` | Latency > p99 or response truncated |
| `correct_wrong_format` | Parsed answer matches but exact match fails |

**Trace capture**: Store compact per-run trace JSON: `{ prompt, raw_output, parsed_answer, tool_calls, timings, failure_mode }`.
*Constraint Fix*: To prevent DB exhaustion on Vercel's 256MB free tier limit, **only** save full traces for failed runs, or keep a rolling window (soft TTL) of the last 10 experiments.

#### Files
- **[MODIFY]** [run.py model](file:///c:/Users/FAZLUL/Desktop/MainProject/LlmForge/backend/app/models/run.py) — add `failure_mode` String column + `trace_data` JSONB column
- **[NEW]** Alembic migration
- **[NEW]** `app/services/failure_classifier.py` — rule-based failure mode classifier
- **[MODIFY]** [experiment_service.py](file:///c:/Users/FAZLUL/Desktop/MainProject/LlmForge/backend/app/services/experiment_service.py) — call classifier after each run, capture trace
- **[MODIFY]** Frontend results grid — add failure mode column + pie chart of failure distribution
- **[NEW]** Frontend trace viewer — expandable panel showing prompt → output → failure reason

