## Phase 6 — Multi-Provider Intelligence (4–5 days)

> Goal: Route inference across free providers with budget awareness.

### 6.1 Budget-Aware Multi-Provider Router & Retry Queue

Provider abstraction layer with routing policies and fallback, plus exponential backoff to handle free-tier API throttling.

**Supported free providers**:
| Provider | Integration | Free Tier Constraints |
|---|---|---|
| HF Inference API | Already built | Rate-limited, heavily throttled on large batches |
| OpenRouter | New adapter | Free models available |
| Groq | New adapter | Strict rate limits (14,400 req/day, low RPM) |

**Routing & Reliability**: `cheapest_first`, `fastest_first`, `fallback_chain`, plus **Exponential Backoff** with jitter (using `tenacity`) to gracefully handle 429 Too Many Requests without crashing the experiment pipeline.

#### Files
- **[NEW]** `app/core/retry.py` — exponential backoff wrappers using `tenacity`
- **[NEW]** `app/services/inference/provider_router.py` — routes requests by policy, handles rate limit errors with fallback
- **[NEW]** `app/services/inference/openrouter_engine.py` — OpenAI-compatible adapter for OpenRouter
- **[NEW]** `app/services/inference/groq_engine.py` — OpenAI-compatible adapter for Groq
- **[NEW]** `app/core/pricing.py` — extend with provider-specific pricing
- **[MODIFY]** [experiment schema](file:///c:/Users/FAZLUL/Desktop/MainProject/LlmForge/backend/app/schemas/experiment.py) — add `provider` field to config
- **[MODIFY]** [experiment_service.py](file:///c:/Users/FAZLUL/Desktop/MainProject/LlmForge/backend/app/services/experiment_service.py) — use router instead of direct engine
- **[MODIFY]** Frontend new experiment form — provider selector dropdown

