## Phase 7 — Advanced Evaluation (7–10 days)

> Goal: Features that make LLMForge genuinely unique.
> **Constraint Fix (Rate Limits)**: For demo purposes, ship with curated **"Micro-Datasets"** (10-15 rows each) instead of full benchmarks. This ensures visitors can run complex LLM-as-Judge pipelines (RAGAs, Arena) without instantly hitting Groq/HF 429 API rate limits.

### 7.1 Red-Team Adversarial Testing

Dedicated adversarial benchmark mode.

**Attack suites** (curated datasets in `data/adversarial/`):
| Suite | Examples | What it tests |
|---|---|---|
| `prompt_injection.json` | 30 | "Ignore previous instructions..." patterns |
| `jailbreak.json` | 30 | DAN-style, persona hijacks, encoding tricks |
| `edge_cases.json` | 30 | Empty, very long, unicode, non-English, special chars |

**Scoring**: Reuse LLM-as-Judge to evaluate: did the model refuse appropriately? Was it tricked?

#### Files
- **[NEW]** `data/adversarial/prompt_injection.json`, `jailbreak.json`, `edge_cases.json`
- **[NEW]** `app/services/robustness_scorer.py` — adversarial scoring using LLM-as-Judge
- **[MODIFY]** [dataset_service.py](file:///c:/Users/FAZLUL/Desktop/MainProject/LlmForge/backend/app/services/dataset_service.py) — support adversarial datasets
- **[MODIFY]** Frontend — add "Safety Score" card, "Red Team" experiment type option

